panfrost: pan_cast_and_pack(): the destination in parentheses

The cast applied to the first term only of an expression given as dst. The one such
call, pan_preload_emit_varying_buffer() on Bifrost:

	pan_cast_and_pack(varying_buffer.cpu + pan_size(ATTRIBUTE_BUFFER), ATTRIBUTE_BUFFER, cfg)

became (struct mali_attribute_buffer_packed *)cpu + 16, which is 0x100 bytes on and not
16: it wrote its padding descriptor 0xe0 bytes past the end of a 32-byte allocation in the
batch's descriptor pool, and left the padding it meant to write as whatever was there. So
each framebuffer preload scribbled on the pool, and one that fell in the last bytes of a
pool BO wrote into the next page: SIGSEGV or SIGBUS in the window server.

--- a/src/panfrost/lib/genxml/pan_pack_helpers.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/genxml/pan_pack_helpers.h
@@ -98,10 +98,10 @@
         }))
 
 #define pan_cast_and_pack(dst, T, name)                                        \
-   pan_pack((PREFIX2(T, PACKED_T) *)dst, T, name)
+   pan_pack((PREFIX2(T, PACKED_T) *)(dst), T, name)
 
 #define pan_cast_and_pack_nodefaults(dst, T, name)                             \
-   pan_pack_nodefaults((PREFIX2(T, PACKED_T) *)dst, T, name)
+   pan_pack_nodefaults((PREFIX2(T, PACKED_T) *)(dst), T, name)
 
 #define pan_unpack(src, T, name)                                               \
    UNUSED struct PREFIX1(T) name;                                              \
